        "explanation": "<p>The hydraulic brake system operates on <b>Pascal's Law</b>, which states that pressure applied to a confined fluid is transmitted undiminished in all directions. This allows force from the brake pedal to be multiplied and transmitted to the wheel cylinders.</p>",
